4. Intake and Triage

One clear front door keeps work visible, routed correctly and measurable.

4.1 Intake Standards

• All requests enter through [intake tool / shared mailbox / portal]. Requests made by chat, email to individual attorneys or hallway conversation are redirected to the front door, unless urgent.
• Every request captures: requester, business unit, request type, description, desired deadline, deal or financial value, and any attachments.
• Business users see a clear description of what Legal can help with and what is available through self-service.

4.2 Triage Process

1.  Acknowledge the request within [1 business day].
2.  Classify by type (contract, advisory, litigation, compliance, employment, IP, privacy, corporate, other) and priority.
3.  Check self-service. If a template, FAQ or playbook answers the request, direct the requester to it.
4.  Assign to the right attorney or queue based on subject matter, workload and conflicts.
5.  Confirm expected timeline with the requester.
6.  Track the request to completion in the system.

