5.2 Required Matter Data

Every matter record should contain, at minimum:
• Matter name, number and type
• Business unit and internal client
• Responsible attorney and team
• Open date, expected close date and actual close date
• Budget, accrual and actual spend
• Outside counsel (if any)
• Status, risk rating and outcome
• Privilege designation
5.3 Matter Hygiene Rules
• Attorneys update status at least [monthly] and after any significant development.
• Matters with no activity in [90 days] are reviewed for closure.
• Closed matters must have an outcome recorded before archiving.
• Legal Ops audits data quality [quarterly] and reports exceptions to practice leads.
6. Outside Counsel Management
6.1 Selection and Panel
• Maintain a preferred panel by practice area and geography, and review it [annually].
• Selection criteria: expertise, results, responsiveness, rates, conflicts, diversity, cultural fit and technology capability.
• Use an RFP or competitive review for significant, recurring or high-cost work.
• New firms are onboarded through Legal Ops: engagement terms, billing guidelines, security and conflicts requirements, and system access.

