6.3 Billing Guidelines (Summary)

Publish and enforce a full set of guidelines. Typical rules include:
• Time entries in [0.1 hour] increments with clear, specific task descriptions
• No block billing
• No billing for clerical or administrative tasks, or for internal training of firm staff
• Pre-approval for expenses above [$ threshold], travel and experts
• Limits on attendees at meetings, depositions and hearings
• Invoices submitted within [30-60 days] of the work period
• Timekeeper changes require prior approval

6.4 Invoice Review Process

1.  Receive invoices through [e-billing system].
2.  Automated checks against rate cards, guidelines and budget.
3.  Legal Ops review for compliance exceptions and adjustments.
4.  Attorney approval of substance and value.
5.  Finance payment within [agreed terms].
6.  Feedback loop. Share adjustments and recurring issues with the firm.

6.5 Performance Reviews

Score firms [annually] or at matter close across the following, and use results in rate talks and panel decisions:
• Quality and outcomes
• Responsiveness and communication
• Budget accuracy and cost control
• Efficiency and staffing
• Billing compliance
• Business understanding
• Diversity and inclusion commitments

