11. Knowledge Management

• Single source of truth for templates, playbooks, precedents, policies and FAQs, in [location].
• Each asset has an owner, last-reviewed date and version.
• Review high-use assets [annually] and immediately after relevant legal or business changes.
• Capture lessons learned at matter close for significant matters; summarize key takeaways in a searchable format.
• Maintain an onboarding pack for new lawyers and business partners that explains how Legal works, how to submit requests and who to contact.

12. Information Governance and Compliance Operations

12.1 Legal Holds

1.  Responsible attorney identifies the duty to preserve.
2.  Legal Ops or the legal coordinator drafts and issues the hold notice to identified custodians.
3.  IT is notified to suspend relevant auto-deletion.
4.  Custodians acknowledge receipt within [5 business days]; non-responders are followed up.
5.  Holds are reviewed [quarterly] and released in writing when no longer needed.
6.  All steps are documented in the matter record.

12.2 Records Retention
• Maintain a retention schedule by record type and jurisdiction, approved by Legal and Compliance.
• Apply schedules consistently across systems.
• Suspend destruction for anything under a legal hold.

12.3 Policy and Training Management
• Central inventory of policies with owner, review date and version.
• Annual attestation and training campaigns, with completion tracked and reported.
• Regulatory change monitoring with a defined path from alert to impact assessment to action.

13. Change Management and Communication
Process and technology changes succeed only if people adopt them.
Change framework
1.  Define the problem, the benefit and who is affected.
2.  Engage stakeholders early; involve end users in design and pilot.
3.  Pilot with a small group; capture feedback and adjust.
4.  Train with short, role-specific guidance and quick-reference materials.
5.  Launch with clear communication about what changes and when.
6.  Reinforce with reminders, champions and visible leadership support.
7.  Measure adoption and outcomes; fix friction quickly.
