14. Implementation Roadmap
First 30 Days: Understand
• Interview the GC, practice leads, Finance and key business stakeholders
• Inventory processes, systems, vendors and spend
• Baseline the starter KPIs
• Identify top pain points and quick wins
Days 31-60: Standardize
• Launch or tighten a single intake channel
• Publish billing guidelines and matter-budget requirements
• Document top contract types and playbook positions
• Clean up matter and contract data in priority areas
Days 61-90: Prove Value
• Release the first operational and spend dashboards
• Run the first outside counsel spend review and rate negotiation
• Launch self-service for one or two high-volume request types
• Present results and a 12-month roadmap to the GC
Months 4-12: Scale
• Roll out or optimize CLM, e-billing and workflow tools based on business case
• Complete annual outside counsel panel review
• Expand self-service and automation
• Introduce quarterly business reviews with key internal clients
• Run a maturity assessment and set next-year goals

